Provenance. This library was first developed for the Lean companion of
L. Chen, I. Ruau and W. Shen, "Chemotaxis models with signal-dependent
sensitivity and a logistic-type source, III: Bifurcation and spike-like
solutions", arXiv:2610.20976. Only the general mathematics is kept here;
nothing in the library depends on the paper.

Dependencies. This library depends on Lean 4 (https://github.com/leanprover/lean4)
and Mathlib (https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4), and through
Mathlib on Batteries, Aesop, Qq (quote4), Plausible, ProofWidgets4,
LeanSearchClient, import-graph and lean4-cli. They are distributed separately
under their own licenses. No upstream source is copied into this repository,
and no authorship of upstream material is claimed.

Related work. The README lists related formalizations by others. No code from
them is used here.

AI assistance. The Lean code was developed with AI assistance under the
author's direction. Every proof is checked by the Lean kernel. The README names
the additional verification tools and the statements they cover.
